From 768b6838327de316ee590570a8d7902cb3dd22dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:59:21 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 wave 30: report page key-equivalent verdicts to the
 host

A Command or Control key-down that reaches page content goes to the renderer
first (RenderWidgetHostViewCocoa performKeyEquivalent: returns YES for every
key equivalent while it is first responder), and an unconsumed one reaches
WebContentsDelegate::HandleKeyboardEvent, which the bridge never overrode: the
key was dropped and the host's menu never saw it. Observe every widget of the
tab (attached in PreHandleKeyboardEvent, before the key is forwarded) and post
the page's acknowledgement to the host: consumed when the page took the key,
otherwise unconsumed, so the host runs its own shortcut. ABI 1.42 / bridge
0.44.0 (key_equivalent_events). Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-04 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
